• Ownership. You keep all rights to your content. ReelSmith claims no ownership of anything you create or post.
• Disconnecting. You can disconnect TikTok at any time in ReelSmith's settings, or revoke access in TikTok under Settings and privacy → Security and permissions → Apps and services permissions.
3. Your data
ReelSmith stores your data on your own computer, not on ReelSmith servers.
• TikTok data. ReelSmith receives only what TikTok's sign-in grants: basic profile information (such as your display name and avatar), the access tokens needed to post, and the posting options TikTok returns for your account. It uses this data only to show which account you're posting to and to upload the videos you choose.
• Storage. Access tokens are kept in your operating system's secure credential store (for example, Windows Credential Manager). Videos, scripts and settings stay in ReelSmith's folder on your computer.
• Sharing. ReelSmith does not sell your data or share it with advertisers. Data is sent only to the services you connect and use (for example, TikTok when you post, or the AI services that generate your scripts, voices and images), under those services' own terms.
• Deleting. Disconnecting TikTok deletes its tokens from your computer. Deleting a video in ReelSmith deletes its files.
